
SENDBUG(1)          UNIX Programmer's Manual           SENDBUG(1)

NAME
     sendbug - mail a system bug report to 2bsd-bugs

SYNOPSIS
     sendbug [ address ]

DESCRIPTION
     Bug reports sent to `2bsd-bugs@BERKELEY' are intercepted  by
     a program which expects bug reports to conform to a standard
     format.  _S_e_n_d_b_u_g is a shell script to help the user  compose
     and  mail  bug reports in the correct format.  _S_e_n_d_b_u_g works
     by invoking _v_i(1) on a temporary copy of the bug report for-
     mat  outline.  The  user must fill in the appropriate fields
     and exit _v_i.  _S_e_n_d_b_u_g then mails  the  completed  report  to
     `2bsd-bugs@BERKELEY' or the address specified on the command
     line.

FILES
     /usr/ucb/bugformat  contains the bug report outline

SEE ALSO
     vi(1)

